<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40925" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rēgŭlus</span></b> ,
			i, m.
		dim.
		rex. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The ruler of a small country</i> (Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυνάστης</span>), <i>a petty
			king</i>, <i>prince</i>, <i>chieftain</i>, <i>lord</i> (freq. in the historians; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">not in Cæs. or Cic.): regulos se
					acceptos in fidem in Hispaniā reges reliquisse,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					37, 25</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Sall. J. 11, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 5,
			38</span></i>; <i><span class="en">27, 4</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">29, 4 al.</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cilicum reguli,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					2, 80</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id.
				Agr. 24</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet. Calig. 5</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Vulg. Josue, 13, 3 al.</span></i>—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> Of <i>the
				king-bee</i>, <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 3, 16,
			18</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A king</i>'<i>s son</i>, <i>a prince</i> (cf. rex and regina), <i><span class="en">Liv. 42,
				24, 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">45,
				14, 6 al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<i>A small bird</i>, Auct. Carm. Phil.
			13.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>D.</b>
			<i>A kind of serpent</i>, <i><span class="en">Hier.
				in Isa. 16, 59, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Prov.
				23, 32</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Isa. 30, 6</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
